# Compile failures

Template parse and validate failures print `error[RCxxxx]:` with a caret
frame. Cite the code from
[diagnostics](/docs/reference/diagnostics/) (`RC2009`, `RC1004`, …), not
only the leading message.

## Generated Roc does not type-check

**Cause:** Rocci parses Roc regions but does not type-check them.

**Fix:** `rocci build FILE`, then use the mapped frame from `rocci run` /
`inspect` segments. Correct the authored expression, not the generated file.

## A directive is rendered as text or a parse error

**Cause:** the `@` form is not at the start of a top-level definition, the
header `{` is on the next line, or markup sits inside `{expr}`.

**Fix:** `rocci inspect --ast FILE`. Compare the header with
[directives](/docs/reference/language/directives/) and
[file structure](/docs/reference/language/file-structure/).

## Still writing the former handler syntax

**Cause:** role-first declarations, pathless `@live`, `@on:METHOD`, and
trailing `json` are **removed**.

**Fix:** rewrite to `@get:view(path)`, `@post:fragment(path)`,
`@post:command(path)`, or `@get:live(path)` as in
[grammar](/docs/reference/language/grammar/).

**Related:** [Diagnostics](/docs/reference/diagnostics/).
